      "raw": "[quote=\"Powerhound_2000\"]\n\nFrom Fireside chats\n<div class=\"bb-quote\">Quote:<br /><blockquote class=\"bb-quote-body\">One-shots are not considered or counted as &ldquo;cards in play.&rdquo; That means Into the Stratosphere or Cedistic Dissonant cannot destroy one-shots that are currently being played.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\n&nbsp;\n\n[/quote]\n\n&nbsp;\n\nIs there a difference between a card &quot;in play&quot; and one &quot;in a play area&quot;? &nbsp; Harvest the Mighty (I think) specifically uses the latter language, unlike Into the Stratosphere/Cedistic Dissonant. &nbsp; If so, then although the one-shots should not be counted to determine the number of cards &quot;in play&quot; (to see who Harvest&#39;s target hero will be), any one-shots that have not yet resolved and are still in a hero&#39;s &quot;play area&quot; should be suitable fodder for Harvest the Mighty. &nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\n\nSounds similar to the difference between &quot;playing a card&quot; and &quot;putting card into play&quot;; effects that prevent the former do not prevent the latter. &nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\n",
