      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/p/b2d939/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2017-01-20T04:42:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>The Buffer Overflow case seems distinct to me. &nbsp;It triggers when a card \"would enter play\" as opposed to other cards that look at \"cards in play\". &nbsp;Even if there is a ruling that one-shots are never considered \"cards in play\", it seem to me they could still \"enter play\". &nbsp;For instance, \"would enter play\" could reasonably be taken as synonymous with \"would be played\", regardless of what type of card it is and what zone it goes to. &nbsp;This isn't to say that the same ruling doesn't apply, it just doesn't seem altogether clear that it should, without being specifically mentioned.</p>",
