      "raw": "<p>The Buffer Overflow case seems distinct to me. &nbsp;It triggers when a card &quot;would enter play&quot; as opposed to other cards that look at &quot;cards in play&quot;. &nbsp;Even if there is a ruling that one-shots are never considered &quot;cards in play&quot;, it seem to me they could still &quot;enter play&quot;. &nbsp;For instance, &quot;would enter play&quot; could reasonably be taken as synonymous with &quot;would be played&quot;, regardless of what type of card it is and what zone it goes to. &nbsp;This isn&#39;t to say that the same ruling doesn&#39;t apply, it just doesn&#39;t seem altogether clear that it should, without being specifically mentioned.</p>",
